ble to every smoke / opt-in story whose live path is external infrastructure: drop the contention burst, replace it with a deterministic redaction-contract branch (httptest.NewServer that echoes a sentinel token; assert the typed wire error AND the absence of the token in the error chain) so the redaction property is enforced on every push and PR even when the live path is skipped. ALSO: the Dokploy client maps a 401/403 from the upstream to `apierr.Internal()` → `yerr.CodeInternal` (Yalla's OWN credentials rejected = internal Yalla misconfiguration, NOT customer-actionable auth failure) — pinning this in the synthetic-server branch is itself a load-bearing contract worth pinning across any future Dokploy-touching smoke.
